{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"The number of spanning trees τ(G), weighted: the sum over spanning trees of the product of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their weights, which is any cofactor of the Laplacian (Kirchhoff’s matrix-tree theorem).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Loops never lie on a tree; parallel edges each count. 0 for the empty graph and for a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"disconnected one, 1 for one vertex. NetworkX ","type":"text"},{"code":"number_of_spanning_trees","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"numberOfSpanningTrees","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"text":": counts pass ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"text":" quickly (K₂₅ has 25²³). The Laplacian with one vertex removed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is eliminated densely as Grassmann, Taksar and Heyman eliminate (each pivot a sum of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conductances, never a difference), so the count keeps a relative accuracy of about n · 10⁻¹⁶","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whatever the weights; its pivots are multiplied with the binary exponent kept apart, so it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"overflows only past ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"text":"’s range, to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".infinity"},{"text":". When every weight is an integer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(unweighted included) and the count is below 2¹⁰⁰, it is computed exactly instead (two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"determinants modulo 62-bit primes, combined by the Chinese remainder theorem) and rounded","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"once, so a count below 2⁵³ is exact. O(n³) time (less on sparse graphs), n² ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"text":"s.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE21numberOfSpanningTreesSdyF","remoteSource":{"fileName":"ElectricalNetworks.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpectralGraphTheory\/ElectricalNetworks.swift#L18"},"symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","modules":[{"name":"SpectralGraphTheory","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"title":"numberOfSpanningTrees()","roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"numberOfSpanningTrees"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"}],"role":"symbol"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/numberofspanningtrees()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/numberOfSpanningTrees()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph","f